{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in compact specification automata. The policy gives priority to forward progress in clear conditions, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, allows one brief backward escape only from a dedicated front-obstacle recovery path, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure state. Action states are one-shot, and uncontrollable events are total in every specification state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capabilities in G so E can enforce safe perception-to-action bindings.",
    "Use forward as the default exploration action, side-specific short turns for ordinary recovery, a rare one-shot backward escape only after front blockage escalation, and full_rotate only from a dedicated last-resort state."
  ],
